  <head>
    <title>US20150372276A1 - Separator for batteries and method of producing separator for batteries 
        - Google Patents</title>

    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="referrer" content="origin-when-crossorigin">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US20150372276A1/en">
    <meta name="description" content="
     A battery separator includes a microporous polyolefin membrane having a thickness of 16 μm or less, and a modifying porous layer comprising a fluorine resin and an inorganic particle or cross-linked polymer particle, the modifying porous layer being laminated on one side of the microporous polyolefin membrane, wherein the microporous polyolefin membrane has (a) a shutdown temperature of 135° C. or lower, and (b) a rate of air resistance change of 1×10 4  sec/100 cc/° C. or more. 
     The separator is suitable for high-capacity batteries, and has adhesion to electrodes and is excellent in shutdown properties and electrolyte permeability. 
   
   ">
    <meta name="DC.type" content="patent">
    <meta name="DC.title" content="Separator for batteries and method of producing separator for batteries 
       ">
    <meta name="DC.date" content="2014-02-12" scheme="dateSubmitted">
    <meta name="DC.description" content="
     A battery separator includes a microporous polyolefin membrane having a thickness of 16 μm or less, and a modifying porous layer comprising a fluorine resin and an inorganic particle or cross-linked polymer particle, the modifying porous layer being laminated on one side of the microporous polyolefin membrane, wherein the microporous polyolefin membrane has (a) a shutdown temperature of 135° C. or lower, and (b) a rate of air resistance change of 1×10 4  sec/100 cc/° C. or more. 
     The separator is suitable for high-capacity batteries, and has adhesion to electrodes and is excellent in shutdown properties and electrolyte permeability. 
   
   ">
